                <pb facs="0474" n="376" xml:id="pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/70: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maginnis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-21T12:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 7:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>84. Carlos Montes requested Legation to take charge of ex-President Montes’
                    private papers. Rumored that new Government may attempt to confiscate Montes’
                    properties, nothing official as yet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Maginnis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
